                <pb facs="0427" n="355" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg355"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister for Foreign Affairs to Minister
                        Heimké.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-07-06"><hi rendition="#italic">July 6,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Heimké</hi>: In reply to your last
                    courteous letter relative to Col. García, who for some time acted as jefe
                    político and comandante de armas of the Department of Izabal I take pleasure in
                    advising you that the substitute, Mr. Luis Estrada Monzón, appointed for the
                    government of that department, has already assumed the duties of his office.</p>
                <p>With my respectful greetings, I remain, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">G. Aguirre.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
